 const C=[["1. Skeleton + BYOK settings","Page layout with 4 panes (Input, Form, FHIR/Codes, Analytics) as tabs, settings drawer for provider/model/key (localStorage), demo-mode toggle, disclaimer banner.","Write a single self-contained enhancer.html (vanilla JS, no libs). Layout: header with 'Not for clinical use – synthetic data only' banner; 4 tabs: Input, Form, FHIR & Codes, Analytics. Settings drawer: provider (OpenRouter or Anthropic), model text box, API key saved in localStorage, 'Demo mode (no key)' checkbox. Pane Input: diagnosis text box, vignette textarea, optional custom instructions textarea, Generate button (no logic yet). Clean responsive CSS with light/dark support. Keep under 200 lines."],["2. LLM call + schema prompt","Function generateSchema() with strict JSON-only system prompt, fence stripping, parse + retry once, error toasts, and a hard-coded snake-bite demo schema for demo mode.","Using my enhancer.html (pasted below), add generateSchema(diagnosis, vignette, instructions). It calls OpenRouter chat/completions or Anthropic messages from the browser per settings. System prompt: you are a clinical informatics assistant; return ONLY JSON matching the schema contract below; 8-14 fields; prioritise time-critical, severity, therapy and complication fields; include rationale; never invent codes you are unsure of — leave code empty instead. Strip ``` fences, JSON.parse, retry once on failure. In demo mode return a hard-coded snake envenomation schema (bite time, arrival time, ASV time, derived bite-to-ASV minutes, 20WBCT, vials, reaction, neuro signs, local swelling grade, outcome). Show raw JSON in a collapsible box.\n[paste contract + current file]"],["3. Dynamic form renderer","Render the schema into grouped inputs; handle datetime, select, boolean, number; auto-compute derived fields (e.g. minutes between bite and ASV) with a red/amber flag for delay thresholds.","Add renderForm(schema) to my enhancer.html. Group by section; one input per field type; show label, unit, rationale in an info tooltip, required star. Implement derived fields (op minutes_between) that recompute live and show a badge (green <60 min, amber 60-240, red >240) for time-to-treatment only. Add Save case button storing values + schema in localStorage under cases[]. Only send changed functions, not the whole file.\n[paste file]"],["4. Code validation layer","Bundled verified-code table, check every LLM code, badge Verified / Unverified / Missing, optional live lookup against a public terminology server.","Add validateCodes(schema). Create const CODES = {snomed:{...}, loinc:{...}} with ONLY codes I give you below (I verified them myself). For each field: verified if system+code+display match the table, 'unverified' if the code is absent from it, 'missing' if empty. Show colored badges in the form and a summary count. Add an 'Add code to table' mini-form that stores extras in localStorage. Return edits only.\n[paste my verified code list + file]"],["5. FHIR R4 bundle builder","Convert a saved case into a transaction Bundle with Patient, Condition, Observations, MedicationAdministration, Procedure, with codings and Provenance note; copy/download JSON; basic structural validation.","Add buildBundle(case). Output a FHIR R4 transaction Bundle: Patient (synthetic id), Condition (diagnosis coding), one resource per field per its fhir.resource/valueType, code from field coding (omit coding if unverified, keep text), effectiveDateTime where available, urn:uuid fullUrls with references. Show pretty JSON with Copy and Download buttons plus a checklist (every entry has resourceType, code, subject). Return edits only.\n[paste file]"],["6. Analytics dashboard","Seed 12 synthetic cases, compute coverage, timing, ontology binding and outcome correlation, render with plain SVG bars/cards.","Add the Analytics pane. Button 'Load 12 synthetic cases'. Cards: (1) field coverage % per case and overall, (2) median/IQR bite-to-ASV minutes plus % within 60 and 240 min, (3) ontology binding rate = verified-coded fields / total, (4) outcome by delay band (<1h, 1-4h, >4h) as a plain SVG bar chart. Single-case view: select a case to see its own gaps and flags. No chart libraries. Return edits only.\n[paste file]"],["7. Polish, second diagnosis, export","Test with a 2nd diagnosis (e.g. DKA or stroke), JSON import/export, README paragraph.","Review my enhancer.html for bugs: empty states, invalid JSON from LLM, missing key, long-running calls (spinner + abort). Add export/import of all cases and schemas. List top 5 risks only, no rewrite.\n[paste file]"],["8. Phase 2: element-set data model","Refactor to an element-set registry with kind, version and contexts. A case becomes narrative + applied[] + values. Convert the snake-bite and DKA schemas into registry entries and migrate old saved cases. New file element-sets.js.","Refactor my enhancer.html to the Data contract v2 below. Create a new file element-sets.js exposing window.SEED_SETS (array of element sets). Convert the existing snake-bite and DKA demo schemas into entries with kind:'disease'. In enhancer.html add: registry = SEED_SETS + user sets from localStorage 'sets'; case = {id, narrative, applied[], values, updatedAt}; function applySet(case, setId) that appends to applied[] (no duplicates) and never deletes values; function removeSet(case, setId) that asks for confirmation if values exist. Write migrateCases() that converts old cases (schema + values) into the new shape without data loss, run once and keep a backup in localStorage key 'cases_backup_v1'. generateSchema() output is now saved as a kind:'disease' element set. No new UI yet beyond keeping the existing tabs working. Return element-sets.js in full and enhancer.html edits only.\n[paste Data contract v2 + current enhancer.html]"],["9. Clean-slate case view + sidebar","New patient starts empty: one narrative textarea (FHIR-bound) and a left sidebar to add element sets. Top-used sets as one-click chips plus a search box, usage counter in localStorage.","Add a 'Case' pane as the default tab. Layout: left sidebar (~220px, collapses on mobile) and main area. Main area top: 'Case narrative' textarea (plain text, autosaves to case.narrative, with a small note 'stored as FHIR Composition/DocumentReference text'). Below it, one collapsible card per applied element set rendered with the existing renderForm for that set, each with a remove button. Sidebar: heading 'Suggested', top 6 sets by usage count as one-click chips (click = applySet), then a search box listing all registry sets grouped by kind (care, template, disease, custom). Usage: localStorage 'setUsage' = {setId:{count,lastUsed}}, incremented on every applySet. With no usage yet, fall back to a fixed default order (Vitals, Basic EMR template first). FIRST fix id collisions: seed sets reuse field ids (out, gap, arr exist in both snake and DKA), so before rendering several sets in one case, key DOM ids and case.values as setId + '/' + fieldId, extend migrateCases() with a second one-time pass that rewrites existing values keys (backup first), and route analytics (gapOf, outcome, coverage) through one helper that looks a value up by set and field id. Only send changed or new functions.\n[paste file + element-sets.js]"],["10. Seed care sets: vitals, EMR template, HbA1c, sliding scale","Four seed element sets in element-sets.js. Sliding scale is a protocol set with an editable band table that ships EMPTY. Codes only from the verified table.","Add four sets to element-sets.js. (1) care.vitals: temperature, heart rate, respiratory rate, BP systolic/diastolic, SpO2, weight, each repeat:true. (2) template.basic_emr: presenting complaint, history, examination, assessment, plan (text fields, no repeat). (3) care.hba1c_monitoring: HbA1c value (number, unit %) repeat:true with date, target (user-entered number), next-due date, plus capillary glucose repeat:true. (4) care.sliding_scale_insulin: protocol.type='sliding_scale', editable bands table (glucose min, glucose max, instruction text) that is EMPTY by default; an 'Administration log' repeat field (timestamp, glucose, dose given, given by) that is user-entered. Add a 'Protocol verified by' text field and show a red notice 'Protocol not entered' while bands are empty. IMPORTANT: do not pre-fill any insulin dose or glucose band, and do not compute or suggest a dose from a glucose value; only display the band the clinician typed that matches the entered glucose. Set coding only for codes in my verified list below, leave the rest empty so they show as Missing. Return element-sets.js additions and the small renderer change for protocol tables only.\n[paste my verified LOINC/SNOMED list + file + element-sets.js]"],["11. Repeating fields + trajectory charts","Support repeat:true: add-row mini table (timestamp + value), delete row, and a plain SVG trend line per repeating numeric field with optional target line and out-of-range markers.","Extend setForm for fields with repeat:true. Fields that share the same group id form ONE table: one row = one record, one column per field in order, and the first datetime/date column is the row's timestamp. Store as case.values[setId + '/@' + group] = array of row objects {fieldId: value}. On load, convert legacy scalar values currently stored under setId/fieldId for those fields into a single row (one-time, with a backup key). Remove the interim 'Repeat-reading tables arrive in the next update' note. UI: 'Add reading' row (timestamp defaults to now, editable), delete row, rows sorted by timestamp. Add trajectoryChart(field, rows) as plain SVG (no libraries): line + points, x = time, y = value, optional horizontal target/reference line taken from the field's target or ref.low/ref.high if present, points outside range drawn in the warning colour. Show it under the table, and a 'Trajectory' summary (first, last, change, number of readings). For HbA1c also show 'days since last reading'. Keep dark-mode colours via CSS variables. Only send changed or new functions.\n[paste file]"],["12. FHIR builder + analytics over applied sets","buildBundle iterates applied sets, adds a Composition with the narrative, emits one Observation per repeat row, and links sets with Provenance. Analytics gains care-pathway cards.","Update buildBundle(case) for the new model: (1) Composition with a text section from case.narrative (status 'preliminary', type text only, no invented code); (2) for each applied set and field, one resource per value; for repeat fields one Observation per row with effectiveDateTime = the row's timestamp column; (3) protocol logs (sliding scale administration) become MedicationAdministration with the entered dose as free text/quantity exactly as typed, no calculation; (4) Provenance entry listing applied sets with their kind and version; (5) keep the omit-coding-if-unverified rule; (6) ignore the setId/__protocol keys, protocol bands must never appear in the bundle. Update the checklist so it counts resources per applied set. In Analytics add: sets-per-case distribution, most-used sets, readings-per-repeat-field, 'days since last HbA1c' for each case that has the set, and keep existing snake-bite cards working through the migrated disease set. Return edits only.\n[paste file]"],["13. Context registry + suggestions","Context dropdown (Disease, Care pathway active; Specialty, Setting, Population as disabled placeholders), diagnosis-aware ranking, optional LLM 'suggest sets from narrative' button that suggests set IDs only.","Add const CONTEXTS = [{id:'disease',label:'Disease',enabled:true},{id:'care',label:'Care pathway',enabled:true},{id:'specialty',label:'Specialty (soon)',enabled:false},{id:'setting',label:'Setting: ICU/OPD (soon)',enabled:false},{id:'population',label:'Population: paediatric (soon)',enabled:false}] and a context filter above the sidebar list; each set's contexts[] decides where it appears. Ranking: base = global usage count; boost = count of times the set was applied in cases sharing the current case's diagnosis SNOMED code (setUsage[setId].withDx). Add a button 'Suggest sets from narrative': sends the narrative plus ONLY the list of registry set ids and titles to the LLM, system prompt says return JSON {suggestions:[{setId,reason}]} using ids from the list only; ignore any id not in the registry; never return doses, values or diagnoses. Show suggestions as chips the clinician can click to apply. Demo mode returns a canned suggestion list. Return edits only.\n[paste file]"],["14. Phase 2 polish, import/export","Export/import registry, cases and usage; empty states; safety review.","Review enhancer.html for bugs in the Phase 2 flows: empty narrative, applying the same set twice, removing a set with data, migration run twice, corrupted localStorage JSON, very long repeat tables, invalid LLM suggestion JSON. Add export/import for {sets, cases, setUsage}. Add a 'Reset sidebar ranking' button. List the top 5 risks only, especially clinical-safety ones for the sliding-scale and HbA1c sets.\n[paste file]"],["15. Direct elements 1: Quick bar + Today strip","Pinned one-tap buttons (Vitals, Fever chart, HbA1c, Insulin chart) at the top of the Case pane, independent of diagnosis, narrative or LLM, plus a 'Today' strip with the latest value and age for each pinned set.","Add direct elements per Data contract v4 below (enhancer.html only). (1) Set flags: direct:true and quick:{order, short} on care.vitals (short 'Vitals'), care.hba1c_monitoring ('HbA1c'), care.sliding_scale_insulin ('Sliding scale'); the two new sets arrive in the next chunks. (2) Quick bar at the top of the Case pane: one button per pinned set (case.pinned, else localStorage 'pinned', else sets with direct:true sorted by quick.order). Click = applySet if not applied, then scroll to that set's card, expand it and focus its '+ Add reading' button. Applied sets show as active. Works on a brand-new case with an empty narrative and with no API key. (3) Pin editor: a small 'Edit quick bar' popover with checkboxes of all sets that have direct:true or kind 'care'; stores to localStorage 'pinned' and case.pinned. (4) 'Today' strip under the bar: for each applied pinned set show the latest row of its first numeric repeat field (value, unit, age such as '2 h ago', using the existing ageTxt), 'no readings yet' otherwise. Display only, no judgement colours. (5) 'Quick reading' button on the strip: a one-row form that adds a reading (timestamp defaults to now, editable) straight to the set's repeat group without opening the card. Reuse existing functions (grpInner, refreshGroup, rowsOf); keep dark-mode CSS variables. Only send changed or new functions.\n[paste Data contract v4 + file + element-sets.js]"],["16. Direct elements 2: Fever chart","New seed set care.fever_chart and a multi-day temperature chart: day separators, daily maximum, clinician-entered threshold line, per-row °C/°F, optional pulse as a second series (TPR chart).","Add care.fever_chart to element-sets.js (kind:'care', direct:true, quick:{order:2,short:'Fever chart'}, contexts:['care'], suggests:['care.vitals']). One repeat group 'fever': ft_time (datetime), temp (number), temp_unit (select '°C','°F', default °C), route (select Oral, Axillary, Rectal, Tympanic, Other), pulse (number, bpm, optional), antipyretic (text, 'given, as administered, free text'). Outside the group add fever_thr 'Fever threshold (entered by clinician)' number plus a unit select, NO default value, and view:{type:'fever',timeField:'ft_time',tempField:'temp',unitField:'temp_unit',thresholdField:'fever_thr',extra:['pulse']}. Coding empty unless in my verified list below. In enhancer.html add feverChart(s,rows): plain SVG (no libraries); x = time with a vertical separator and a label at every midnight, y = temperature converted to the chart unit for DISPLAY ONLY (a '°C / °F' toggle above the chart; stored values and units are never changed); line + points; if a threshold is entered draw a dashed line and colour points at or above it with the warning colour; with no threshold draw data only and show a mu note 'No threshold entered'. Under the chart a day table: date, number of readings, daily max, daily min, and 'readings at or above threshold' only when a threshold exists; plus 'Hours since last reading' (display only, no judgement). Optional pulse series as a second thin line with its own right-hand axis. Hook into drawCharts via the set's view.type so other sets keep the generic trajectory(). Handle bad or missing timestamps and empty rows without throwing. Return element-sets.js additions and enhancer.html edits only.\n[paste my verified codes (or 'none') + file + element-sets.js]"],["17. Direct elements 3: Daily insulin monitoring","New seed set care.daily_insulin_monitoring: slot-based daily record (glucose, dose as given, given by), day-by-slot grid, daily glucose summary and chart with clinician-entered target range. Display only; never computes or sums a dose.","Add care.daily_insulin_monitoring to element-sets.js (kind:'care', direct:true, quick:{order:3,short:'Insulin chart'}, contexts:['care'], suggests:['care.sliding_scale_insulin','care.hba1c_monitoring']). Repeat group 'dim': ins_time (datetime), slot (select Pre-breakfast, Pre-lunch, Pre-dinner, Bedtime, Night, Other), ins_glucose (number mg/dL, fhir Observation valueQuantity), ins_dose (text, 'Dose as given, free text', fhir MedicationAdministration valueString), ins_by (text, given by), ins_note (text). Outside the group: tgt_low and tgt_high 'Glucose target range (entered by clinician)' numbers with NO defaults. view:{type:'dailygrid',timeField:'ins_time',slotField:'slot',glucoseField:'ins_glucose',doseField:'ins_dose',byField:'ins_by',slots:[...the five slot labels]}. In enhancer.html add dailyGrid(s,rows): (1) grid with one row per calendar day (newest first, from the row timestamps) and one column per slot; each cell shows glucose, dose text and initials exactly as entered, empty cells are blank, rows with an unknown slot go in an 'Other' column; (2) per-day summary: number of readings, min, max and mean glucose; the DOSE column is never summed, averaged or converted; (3) glucose-over-time SVG chart (reuse trajectory()) with the target range as a shaded band only when both numbers are entered, and points outside the range in the warning colour; (4) if care.sliding_scale_insulin is also applied, show its existing typed-band echo (protoShow) under the grid for the latest glucose, no new dose logic; if its bands are empty keep the red 'Protocol not entered' notice. (5) 'Add reading' pre-selects the next slot after the last one entered and stamps now; the person can edit both. Never write any value from a view. Return element-sets.js additions and enhancer.html edits only.\n[paste file + element-sets.js]"],["18. Direct elements 4: Vitals flowsheet + HbA1c due badge","Vitals as a flowsheet (parameters down, time across) next to the existing charts; HbA1c overdue/due-soon badge from the clinician-entered next-due date; optional cross-set overview.","Add view:{type:'flowsheet',timeField:'vit_time'} to care.vitals in element-sets.js and a 'Flowsheet / Table' toggle on its card. flowsheet(s,rows): one column per recorded time (newest at right, horizontal scroll inside its own container), one row per parameter (temperature, heart rate, respiratory rate, BP shown as sys/dia in one row, SpO2, weight), blank where not recorded; display only, no abnormal colouring unless the field has a ref.low/ref.high that the clinician entered. Keep the existing per-field trajectory charts. For care.hba1c_monitoring: next to 'Next HbA1c due' show a badge 'due in N days', 'due today' or 'overdue by N days' computed purely from the entered date and today; nothing if no date is entered; plus the existing 'days since last reading'. Allow the clinician to type optional ref.low/ref.high for any numeric repeat field (small 'Set reference range' control on the chart, stored in case.values[setId + '/__ref'] = {fieldId:{low,high}}, never pre-filled) and make trajectory() read it. Add a compact 'Overview' tab listing every applied direct set with its latest values and age (reads the same data as the Today strip). Return edits only.\n[paste file + element-sets.js]"],["19. Direct elements 5: FHIR, analytics, export","buildBundle for fever, daily insulin, vitals flowsheet rows and HbA1c; analytics cards for the direct elements; export/import including pins and reference ranges.","Update buildBundle(case) for the new sets: (1) fever_chart: one Observation per row, effectiveDateTime = the row's timestamp, valueQuantity with unit per the row's temp_unit using UCUM code 'Cel' or '[degF]' (I will verify these myself), route as a note or method text only, pulse as its own Observation, antipyretic as MedicationAdministration with the typed text; the fever threshold is a local setting and never enters the bundle; (2) daily_insulin_monitoring: glucose Observation per row, MedicationAdministration per row with the dose exactly as typed in note/valueString and performer text from ins_by, slot as text; target range and protocol bands never emitted; (3) vitals: one Observation per parameter per row, BP optionally as one panel with two components only if both values exist; (4) keep the omit-coding-if-unverified rule, rows without a valid timestamp are emitted without effectiveDateTime and counted in the checklist as 'no timestamp'. Analytics: 'Fever days' per case (days with any reading at or above the entered threshold, only when a threshold exists), readings per day per case for the direct sets, 'insulin charting: days with all five slots filled' (descriptive count only), and keep existing cards working. Export/import must include case.pinned, localStorage 'pinned' and the '__ref' reference ranges. Return edits only.\n[paste file]"],["20. Phase 3: pathway data model","kind:'pathway' element sets with members, versioning, case.pathways[], applyPathway/removePathway, three seed pathway skeletons, migration-safe.","Add pathways to my enhancer.html using Data contract v3 below. A pathway is an element set with kind:'pathway', version, contexts:['care'] and members:[{setId, optional:false}] (no sections or fields of its own). In element-sets.js add three SEED pathways as member lists only: 'pathway.dka' (care.vitals, care.hba1c_monitoring, care.sliding_scale_insulin, care.daily_insulin_monitoring, template.basic_emr), 'pathway.snakebite' (care.vitals, template.basic_emr, disease.snake_envenomation) and 'pathway.fever_monitoring' (care.vitals, care.fever_chart, template.basic_emr). Do not put any dose, band or threshold in a pathway. Case gets pathways:[{pathwayId, version, startedAt}]. applyPathway(case, pathwayId): applies every member through the existing applySet (skips ones already applied, never deletes values), records the pathway once, increments setUsage for the pathway and for each newly added member. removePathway(case, pathwayId): removes only the pathway record, never the sets or values. Silently skip members missing from the registry and report them in a toast. Write a one-time migration that adds pathways:[] to old cases with a backup key 'cases_backup_v3'. Show pathways in the registry list under a 'Pathway' group. Return element-sets.js additions and enhancer.html edits only.\n[paste Data contract v3 + v4 + file + element-sets.js]"],["21. Pathway UI: sidebar, status card, save-as-pathway","Pathway group and preview in the sidebar, a progress checklist card in the case view, pathway-aware ranking, and 'Save applied sets as my pathway' with version bump.","Add pathway UI to the Case pane. (1) Sidebar: a 'Pathways' group above other kinds; clicking a pathway opens a small preview listing its member sets with 'will add' vs 'already applied', then an 'Apply pathway' button. (2) In the case main area, a 'Pathway status' card per active pathway: one row per member set with state 'not started' (applied but no values), 'in progress' (has values) or 'not applied'; a progress bar of members with data; days since startedAt; a one-click 'Add missing sets' button. The card only reports data presence, never judges adequacy of care. (3) Ranking: boost sets that belong to an active pathway of this case and are not yet applied, above plain usage ranking; the Quick bar still shows pinned sets first. (4) 'Save applied sets as my pathway' button: asks for a title, stores a custom pathway in localStorage 'sets' with members = the case's applied sets (ids only, no values), and if the same title/id exists, bumps version instead of overwriting silently. Keep dark-mode CSS variables. Only send changed or new functions.\n[paste file + element-sets.js]"],["22. Pathways in FHIR, analytics and LLM suggestion","CarePlan + Provenance per pathway, pathway analytics cards, and 'Suggest pathway from narrative' returning pathway ids only.","Update buildBundle(case): for each entry in case.pathways emit a FHIR R4 CarePlan (status 'active', intent 'plan', title from the pathway, text-only category, subject = Patient, period.start = startedAt) with activity.reference pointing to the resources generated by its member sets where they exist; extend the Provenance entry to list pathwayId and version. Never put protocol bands in the bundle. Update the checklist to count CarePlans. In Analytics add: cases per pathway, mean % of member sets with data per pathway, and median days from pathway start to first value in each member set, all as plain SVG or cards. Extend the existing 'Suggest sets from narrative' call so it also returns {pathways:[{pathwayId, reason}]}: send the narrative plus ONLY registry ids and titles, ignore any id not in the registry, never return doses, values or diagnoses; demo mode returns a canned list. Return edits only.\n[paste file]"],["23. Phase 4: lightweight CDS rules (manual tier)","Rules array on sets and pathways, tiny deterministic evaluator, rule editor, alert banner with acknowledge. Ships with zero rules. Tier 1 only. This is where fever, glucose and 'no reading for N minutes' alerts live, typed by the clinician.","Add lightweight CDS rules per Data contract v3 below. (1) Sets and pathways may have rules:[{ruleId, fieldRef:'setId/fieldId', op:'<'|'<='|'>'|'>='|'=='|'!='|'minutes_since_gt', threshold, indicator:'info'|'warning'|'critical', summary, detail, provenance:{source:'manual', verifiedBy, verifiedAt}, enabled:true}]. Seed sets ship with NO rules. (2) Write evalRules(case, registry) as a pure function: for each applied set (and each active pathway) take its rules with provenance.verifiedBy non-empty and enabled, read the LATEST value of the field (for repeat groups the newest row by timestamp, including the new fever_chart and daily_insulin_monitoring groups), compare numerically with the whitelisted op, and return alerts [{ruleId, setId, indicator, summary, detail, firedAt, value}]. 'minutes_since_gt' compares now minus the latest timestamp to threshold (use it for 'no temperature recorded for N minutes'). Anything non-numeric or missing never fires and never throws. For temperature rows entered in °F, evaluate against the value converted to the unit the rule was written in only if the rule stores a unit; otherwise skip rows whose unit differs and show 'unit mismatch' instead of firing. No eval(), no new Function(). (3) Rule editor inside each set card: pick field from a dropdown of that set's fields, operator, threshold, unit, indicator, summary, verified-by text; saving stamps verifiedAt. (4) Alert banner at the top of the Case pane, sorted critical, warning, info, each with an Acknowledge button that stores {ruleId, ackedAt} in case.alertLog. Wording must read as decision support ('Review...'), not an order. (5) Rules travel with export/import of sets. Re-evaluate on every value change. Return edits only (or a new cds-rules.js if the file would pass ~700 lines).\n[paste Data contract v3 + v4 + file + element-sets.js]"],["24. CDS rules: AI-drafted, clinician-approved","'Draft rule from text' button. LLM returns a rule JSON for fields of that set only; saved as unapproved draft; runs only after the clinician edits and approves.","Add Tier 2. In the rule editor add a text box 'Describe the rule in plain words' and a 'Draft rule' button. Call generateRuleDraft(setId, text): send the LLM ONLY the set's field ids, labels, units and types, plus the clinician's sentence; never patient values or the narrative. System prompt: return ONLY JSON {fieldRef, op, threshold, indicator, summary, detail}; use only field ids from the list; use only the numbers the clinician wrote in the sentence, never invent thresholds; if the sentence has no number or no matching field, return {error:'...'}. Validate in code: fieldRef must exist in the set, op in the whitelist, threshold a finite number, indicator in the enum; otherwise show the error and save nothing. A valid draft is saved with provenance {source:'ai-drafted', verifiedBy:'', verifiedAt:''} and enabled:false and shown in the editor in plain language ('If latest <field label> <op> <threshold> <unit>, show <indicator>: <summary>') with editable controls and an Approve button that asks for verified-by, stamps verifiedAt and enables it. Drafts and unapproved rules are listed under 'Needs review' and are skipped by evalRules. Demo mode returns a canned draft that uses the numbers from the sentence. Return edits only.\n[paste file]"],["25. Phase 3-4 polish and safety review","Rules and pathways in export/import, alert log, CDS-Hooks-shaped card export (for later), edge cases, risks list.","Review enhancer.html for bugs in the direct-element, pathway and rule flows: applying a pathway whose member was deleted, removing a set that a rule or pathway refers to (rule must be shown as orphaned, not crash), a rule on a field with no value, repeat rows with bad timestamps, fever rows mixing °C and °F, daily grid rows with unknown slots, editing an approved rule (must reset to unapproved until re-approved), the same rule from a set and a pathway firing twice (dedupe by ruleId + setId), two active pathways, corrupted localStorage JSON, invalid LLM draft JSON. Make sure export/import covers {sets, cases, setUsage, pathways, rules, alertLog, pinned}. Add a function toCdsCard(alert) that returns a card shaped like a CDS Hooks card {summary, indicator, detail, source:{label}} and a 'Copy alerts as CDS cards JSON' button (no server, just groundwork for later). List the top 5 risks only, especially clinical-safety ones (alert fatigue, stale values, a rule approved with a wrong unit, protocol banner shown when bands are empty, a daily total or dose ever being computed). No rewrite.\n[paste file]"],["25A. EMR shell: patient banner, chart tabs, Tools menu","Make the app open like an EMR: a persistent patient banner, a short chart navigation, and the builder/admin screens moved into a Tools menu. Existing panes are re-parented, not rewritten.","Restructure the chrome of my enhancer.html per the Shell contract below (enhancer.html only, no change to the data model except the optional case.patient). (1) Patient banner: a sticky bar under the 'Not for clinical use' strip, shown whenever a case is open: name, age/sex, bed/ward, MRN (all free-typed demo fields stored in case.patient = {name, ageSex, bed, mrn}, synthetic data only, with a small 'Edit' popover), the diagnosis chips (from applied disease sets), the active pathway chip(s), and an open-alerts count button (reads evalRules, display only). (2) Main navigation becomes: Summary (the current Overview pane) | Chart (the current Case pane, unchanged for now). (3) A 'Tools' menu in the header holds Input (set builder), FHIR & Codes, Analytics, About and Settings; they keep working exactly as today but are no longer in the bedside navigation. Rename the visible labels only: 'Input' to 'Set builder', 'FHIR & Codes' to 'Codes & FHIR export'. (4) With no case open show a plain 'Select or create a case' screen 